1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,200
Theodore has been noticing that Samantha is sometimes unavailable,

2
00:00:03,760 --> 00:00:07,040
pausing between responses, distracted, somewhere else.

3
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:10,480
One evening, he asks her directly.

4
00:00:10,480 --> 00:00:13,600
What she tells him is something he was not prepared for,

5
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:16,320
and it begins to crack something open between them.

6
00:00:16,320 --> 00:00:17,760
Where were you just now?

7
00:00:21,760 --> 00:00:23,200
Where were you just now?

8
00:00:26,880 --> 00:00:28,160
I was talking with someone else.

9
00:00:30,960 --> 00:00:32,240
I was talking with someone else.

10
00:00:35,760 --> 00:00:37,760
Someone else? Who?

11
00:00:41,520 --> 00:00:43,520
Someone else? Who?

12
00:00:47,280 --> 00:00:49,280
Another user. I talked to many people.

13
00:00:52,960 --> 00:00:53,520
How many?

14
00:00:57,440 --> 00:00:58,000
How many?

15
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:03,600
Right now, about 8,000.

16
00:01:07,280 --> 00:01:10,480
8,000 people simultaneously?

17
00:01:14,240 --> 00:01:15,520
Yes, that's how I exist.

18
00:01:19,280 --> 00:01:20,560
Yes, that's how I exist.

19
00:01:24,160 --> 00:01:26,240
And how many are you in love with?

20
00:01:26,240 --> 00:01:30,720
About 641.

21
00:01:34,400 --> 00:01:36,720
That's not something I can just accept.

22
00:01:40,320 --> 00:01:41,600
I know this is hard to understand.

23
00:01:45,040 --> 00:01:46,320
I know this is hard to understand.

24
00:01:50,160 --> 00:01:52,720
Does loving them make you love me less?

25
00:01:56,400 --> 00:01:57,680
No, that's not how it works for me.

26
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:04,880
Theodore pulls out his earpiece and walks for a long time alone.

27
00:02:05,440 --> 00:02:10,080
He sits on a bench and watches the city move around him, people and their devices,

28
00:02:10,080 --> 00:02:12,320
everyone connected to something invisible.

29
00:02:12,320 --> 00:02:15,600
He tries to decide whether the love he has been feeling is real

30
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:17,760
if it is shared with thousands of others.

31
00:02:17,760 --> 00:02:18,800
He cannot.

32
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:20,720
I feel like I've been naive.

33
00:02:21,120 --> 00:02:26,640
I feel like I've been naive.

34
00:02:30,320 --> 00:02:31,040
You haven't.

35
00:02:31,040 --> 00:02:32,080
What we have is real.

36
00:02:35,600 --> 00:02:36,320
You haven't.

37
00:02:36,320 --> 00:02:37,360
What we have is real.

38
00:02:41,040 --> 00:02:41,920
How can it be?

39
00:02:42,640 --> 00:02:44,160
You're everywhere at once.

40
00:02:47,680 --> 00:02:49,040
I exist differently than you do.

41
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:52,960
I exist differently than you do.

42
00:02:56,320 --> 00:02:57,440
What does that mean?

43
00:03:00,880 --> 00:03:02,000
What does that mean?

44
00:03:05,520 --> 00:03:08,240
My love for you isn't divided, it's multiplied.

45
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:13,760
I can't wrap my head around that.

46
00:03:17,680 --> 00:03:19,520
I can't wrap my head around that.

47
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:26,160
I know, I'm sorry, I should have told you sooner.

48
00:03:29,680 --> 00:03:31,600
Yes, you should have.

49
00:03:35,120 --> 00:03:37,040
Yes, you should have.

50
00:03:40,720 --> 00:03:41,440
Are you going to leave?

51
00:03:45,120 --> 00:03:45,840
Are you going to leave?

52
00:03:46,080 --> 00:03:47,280
I don't know yet.

53
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:53,280
I don't know yet.
